<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">equipment</ansi>

All unworn items belong to company cargo. Each member keeps their worn gear.
Assign equipment before a fight; no gear changes or item use are allowed in battle.

  company equipment
  Lists cargo items and their exact references, such as !10004:[instance].
  Copy the full reference when several items have the same name.

  company compare [member] [item]
  Shows hands, reach, price, protection, shield changes, worn weight,
  personal burden and company capacity before you assign it. Check the
  member's strategy role; higher price alone does not mean better gear.

  company equip [member] [item]
  company equip [member] [exact-reference] [slot]
  Equips one cargo item and returns displaced equipment to shared cargo.
  Use leader (or me) for yourself, #1 for companion 1, or a quoted member name.
  The companion must be alive, present, and still yours. With an exact
  reference, add weapon or offhand to choose that hand explicitly.

  company remove [member] [slot]
  Returns worn gear to cargo. Slots include weapon, offhand, head, neck,
  body, belt, gloves, ring, legs, feet and pack.

A two-handed weapon removes the offhand; a shield displaces a two-handed
weapon. Disabled slots, bound gear and curses can prevent an assignment.
Cargo must fit after the change. Capacity-restoring assignments are allowed
while overloaded; removing a pack preserves cargo and can leave it overloaded.
Assigned packs add capacity, not combat burden (help pack).
Nothing is duplicated or automatically upgraded. There are no equipment presets.

The legacy equip/wear/wield and remove commands manage the leader only.
gearup directs you to deliberate assignment rather than choosing by price.
In Company > Inventory, click cargo gear to compare or assign it to a member;
Character > Gear is your equipment editor. Select a slot (including Pack),
then a compatible exact cargo item to preview it. Current → After shows weapon
damage dice, active edge bonus/remaining strikes for each hand, hands, reach, shield, protection, worn weight, burden, dodge retained,
core stats, maximum health/mana and company capacity/cargo. Actual damage still
depends on the foe and combat conditions; burden reduces dodge, not combat speed.
Displaced gear is listed before you apply the change. Preview removal to see its
impact, then choose Remove equipment. Empty slots and unavailable choices show
why; if an item changes or leaves cargo, select again. Commands revalidate the
exact item when you act. Companion gear remains managed through company commands.
Text and browser use the same checks.

Gear can come with a quality, a rarity, affixes and a level requirement
(<ansi fg="command">help rarity</ansi>): equip and compare refuse a member who is too low, and say
what level it needs. Rare gear is read with <ansi fg="command">help scribe</ansi>.

Weapons and armor come in families and tiers, from padded cloth and iron to
steel and tempered gear: <ansi fg="command">help equipmenttiers</ansi>. Goods you carry to sell are in <ansi fg="command">help goods</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help equipmenttiers</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help goods</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help cargo</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help treasury</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help loot</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help rarity</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help quality</ansi>,
